       <div class="col-lg-8">
             <img class="blog-hero-image" src="data:image/webp;base64," alt="AP Inter Hall Ticket 2026">
             <div class="blog-content">
                <div class="blog-body">
                    <h1 class="blog-title text-center mb-4">AP Inter Hall Ticket 2026: Your Gateway to the Intermediate Public Exams is Here!</h1>
                    <p class="lead text-center mb-5">The Board of Intermediate Education, Andhra Pradesh (BIEAP) is all set to release the much-awaited AP Inter Hall Tickets 2026. Students across the state are eagerly anticipating their admit cards, which are essential for appearing in the upcoming Intermediate Public Examinations (IPE).</p>

                    <div class="section-title">Key Highlights for AP Inter Hall Ticket 2026</div>
                    <div class="subsection-paragraph benefit-card">
                        <p>✅ **Release Status:** Theory exam hall tickets expected to be released between February 11th and 15th, 2026, with a strong possibility of activation on February 12th.</p>
                        <p>✅ **Official Download Portals:** bie.ap.gov.in and bieap.apcfss.in are the primary websites.</p>
                        <p>✅ **Alternative Access:** Hall tickets can also be obtained via the Mana Mitra WhatsApp service at 9552300009.</p>
                        <p>✅ **Exam Dates:** 1st Year exams from February 23 to March 24, 2026; 2nd Year exams from February 24 to March 23, 2026.</p>
                        <p>✅ **Mandatory Document:** Carrying your hall ticket to the examination center is compulsory.</p>
                    </div>

                    <p>With the practical examinations already concluded on February 10, 2026, the focus now shifts to the theory exams. Over 10 lakh students are expected to appear for the AP Inter Public Exams this year, highlighting the significant scale of these examinations.</p>

                    <div class="section-title">AP Inter Hall Ticket 2026: Expected Release and How to Download</div>
                    <p>The Board of Intermediate Education, Andhra Pradesh (BIEAP), is preparing to release the AP Inter Hall Tickets 2026 for both 1st and 2nd-year students imminently. While an exact time has not been officially declared, trends suggest the admit cards could be live anytime between February 11th and February 15th, 2026, with many anticipating the release on February 12th.</p>

                    <div class="benefit-item">
                        <div class="benefit-title">1. Downloading from Official Websites</div>
                        <div class="benefit-content">
                            <p>Once released, students can follow these steps to download their hall tickets from the official BIEAP websites:</p>
                            <ol>
                                <li>Visit the official websites: <a href="https://bie.ap.gov.in" target="_blank">bie.ap.gov.in</a> or <a href="https://bieap.apcfss.in" target="_blank">bieap.apcfss.in</a>.</li>
                                <li>Look for the link titled "AP Inter Hall Ticket 2026 Download" or "Theory Hall Ticket February 2026 Download" on the homepage.</li>
                                <li>You may need to select your stream (General/Vocational) if prompted.</li>
                                <li>Enter the required login credentials, which typically include your Roll Number / Registration Number / Previous Hall Ticket Number / SSC Hall Ticket Number (for 1st year) and Date of Birth. An Aadhaar number might also be required.</li>
                                <li>Complete the Captcha verification if present.</li>
                                <li>Click on the 'Download' or 'Submit' button.</li>
                                <li>Your AP Inter Hall Ticket 2026 will be displayed on the screen. Verify all details carefully.</li>
                                <li>Download the hall ticket and take at least two or three printouts for future reference.</li>
                            </ol>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="benefit-item">
                        <div class="benefit-title">2. Accessing via Mana Mitra WhatsApp Service</div>
                        <div class="benefit-content">
                            <p>In a convenient digital initiative, BIEAP also provides the option to download your hall ticket through their Mana Mitra WhatsApp service.</p>
                            <ol>
                                <li>Save the official BIEAP WhatsApp number: <strong>9552300009</strong> to your phone contacts.</li>
                                <li>Open WhatsApp and send a "Hi" message to the BIEAP contact.</li>
                                <li>Follow the prompts and select the option for "Educational Services" and then "download intermediate hall ticket 2026".</li>
                                <li>Provide your Aadhaar number or previous hall ticket number and Date of Birth when requested.</li>
                                <li>The downloadable PDF of your AP Intermediate admit card 2026 will be sent to you.</li>
                            </ol>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="highlight-text">
                        <strong>Note:</strong> Some reports suggest that while students can download hall tickets from official portals, schools also play a role in downloading, verifying, and distributing physical copies. It is advisable to also check with your respective school or college.
                    </div>

                    <div class="section-title">Important Dates at a Glance: AP Inter Exams 2026</div>
                    <p>Be prepared with the complete schedule for the AP Intermediate Public Examinations 2026:</p>
                    <table>
                        <thead>
                            <tr>
                                <th>Event</th>
                                <th>1st Year (Class 11)</th>
                                <th>2nd Year (Class 12)</th>
                            </tr>
                        </thead>
                        <tbody>
                            <tr>
                                <td>Practical Exams</td>
                                <td colspan="2">February 1 - February 10, 2026 (9 AM-12 PM &amp; 2 PM-5 PM)</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td>Theory Exams Start Date</td>
                                <td>February 23, 2026</td>
                                <td>February 24, 2026</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td>Theory Exams End Date</td>
                                <td>March 24, 2026</td>
                                <td>March 23, 2026</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td>Exam Timings</td>
                                <td colspan="2">9:00 AM to 12:00 Noon (Single Shift)</td>
                            </tr>
                             <tr>
                                <td>Ethics and Human Values Exam</td>
                                <td colspan="2">January 21, 2026 (10:00 AM to 1:00 PM)</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td>Environmental Education Exam</td>
                                <td colspan="2">January 23, 2026 (10:00 AM to 1:00 PM)</td>
                            </tr>
                        </tbody>
                    </table>
                    <p class="small text-muted"><em>Note: Some exam dates were rescheduled. The AP Inter 2nd year exam originally on March 3rd is now on March 4th, 2026. The AP Inter 1st year exam originally on March 20th is now on March 21st, 2026.</em></p>


                    <div class="section-title">Crucial Details to Verify on Your Hall Ticket</div>
                    <div class="subsection-paragraph benefit-card">
                        <p>✅ Your Name and Parent's Name</p>
                        <p>✅ Roll Number and Registration Number</p>
                        <p>✅ Photograph and Signature</p>
                        <p>✅ Subject Names and Codes</p>
                        <p>✅ Examination Centre Name and Address</p>
                        <p>✅ Exam Dates and Timings for Each Subject</p>
                        <p>✅ Important Instructions for Exam Day</p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="section-title">Addressing Discrepancies in Your Admit Card</div>
                    <div class="benefit-item">
                        <div class="benefit-title">What to do if you find an error?</div>
                        <div class="benefit-content">
                            <p>It is crucial to meticulously check all the details on your downloaded AP Inter Hall Ticket 2026. In case you find any discrepancy, such as an incorrect name, photograph, or subject details, immediately inform your respective school principal.</p>
                            <p>Corrections, if required, will be processed through the Regional Inspection Officer (RIO) or the District Intermediate Education Officer (DIEO) before the commencement of the examination.</p>
                            <p>If your photo on the printed hall ticket is pixelated or unidentifiable, try re-downloading. If the issue persists, contact your school/college principal.</p>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="section-title">Why Your Hall Ticket is Indispensable</div>
                    <div class="subsection-paragraph benefit-card">
                        <p>✅ **Entry Pass:** It is the mandatory document for gaining entry into the examination hall on all exam days.</p>
                        <p>✅ **Identity Proof:** Serves as proof of your identity as a registered candidate for the exams.</p>
                        <p>✅ **Exam Details:** Contains vital information about your exam centre, subjects, and schedule.</p>
                        <p>✅ **Future Reference:** Essential for checking results and for other academic procedures.</p>
                    </div>

                    <p>As the AP Inter Exams 2026 draw near, students are advised to keep their hall tickets safely and review all instructions mentioned on them. Best of luck to all the candidates!</p>
                </div>
            </div>
       </div>

            
            
